    "text": {
     "en": "This poem wonders where the bright Sun goes at night.\nIt tells us that the Sun sinks behind a distant hill, and the world grows dark and still.\nThen the child goes to bed and sleeps until the day begins to peep.\nWhen the child opens their eyes the Sun is shining again.\nThe Sun does not really go away. The Earth turns, so we have day and night (additional, not in the textbook).\nNew words: wonder, distant, peep.\nThink about colours at sunrise and sunset, and what you see in the night sky."
    }
